---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import CarouselBuild from "../../components/UnderTheHood/CarouselBuild.astro"
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro"
---

<TechniquePost slug="carousel-css-only">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      Scroll snap made swiping between slides a CSS job years ago. The controls
      never were: previous and next buttons, dots that show where you are, and
      disabling the buttons at either end all needed JavaScript that listens to
      scroll events and keeps state in sync.
    </p>
    <p>
      Those controls also had to be made accessible by hand: labels, focus and
      the current slide.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A grid with <code>grid-auto-flow: column</code> and <code
          >scroll-snap-type</code
        > is the track
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>::scroll-button()</code> generates real, focusable buttons that scroll
        the track and disable themselves at the ends
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>::scroll-marker</code> gives every item a dot inside a <code
          >::scroll-marker-group</code
        >, and <code>:target-current</code> styles the active one
      </li>
      <li>
        The alt text in <code>content: "" / "Next"</code> names the buttons, a CSS
        counter numbers the dots
      </li>
      <li>Anchor positioning places the buttons over the scroller</li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`.carousel {
  counter-reset: item;
  scroll-marker-group: after;
  scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
}

.carousel::scroll-button(inline-end) {
  content: "" / "Next";
  inset-block-start: anchor(center);
  inset-inline-end: calc(anchor(self-end) + 0.5rem);
  position: absolute;
  position-anchor: auto;
}

.carousel > * {
  counter-increment: item;
  scroll-snap-align: start;
}

.carousel > *::scroll-marker {
  content: "" / "Slide " counter(item);
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <CarouselBuild />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Without the pseudo-elements there are no buttons or dots, just a scroll
        snapping row you swipe or scroll
      </li>
      <li>
        The scrollbar is only hidden inside <code
          >@supports selector(::scroll-button(*))</code
        >, so it stays as the control elsewhere
      </li>
      <li>
        Space for buttons outside the items is only reserved under the same
        check
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
